      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the original test. It has several understandability problems:\n- Uses undefined generic type `E` in a non-generic class\n- Has uncompilable abstract method stubs (`__super_makeEmptyIterator`, `__super_makeObject`)\n- Contains helper methods and setup that are unused by the actual test\n- Has numerous unused imports\n\nI'll create a clean, focused version that preserves the exact runtime behaviour.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all dead code (undefined generic type `E`, uncompilable abstract method stubs, unused helper methods and imports), replaces the raw type with concrete `String`, and adds clear comments explaining the bounded window parameters — all while preserving the exact same method calls and assertions as the original `testRemoveMiddle` test."
